# Feature Development Guidelines

## MVP Feature Scope
Based on the [PRD](mdc:docs/PRD.md), implement these core features in order of priority:

### 1. Authentication (Critical)
- Email/password signup and login
- Google SSO integration
- Password reset flow
- Session persistence and logout
- Route protection for authenticated users

### 2. User Profiles (Critical)
- Profile creation and editing (name, username, photo, bio)
- Profile viewing from chat interfaces
- Avatar management with image uploads

### 3. Direct Messaging (Critical)
- 1-on-1 conversations between users
- Real-time text and image messaging
- Message history persistence
- User search and conversation initiation

### 4. Group Chat (High Priority)
- Multi-participant chat rooms
- Room creation, joining, and leaving
- Member management and invitations
- Group messaging with same features as DMs

### 5. Real-time Presence (High Priority)
- Online/away status indicators
- Typing indicators within conversations
- Real-time status updates

### 6. Push Notifications (Medium Priority)
- FCM integration for background notifications
- In-app notification banners
- Unread message badge counts
- Notification preferences

### 7. Admin Functionality (Low Priority)
- Admin dashboard for user and room management
- Content moderation tools
- User removal capabilities

## Development Approach
- **Feature-First**: Implement complete vertical slices
- **Real-time First**: Use Firebase real-time listeners throughout
- **Mobile-First**: Design for mobile, enhance for desktop
- **Error-Resilient**: Implement comprehensive error handling

## Technical Specifications
Each feature has detailed technical specs in `docs/features/*/`:
- [Authentication](mdc:docs/features/authentication/authentication.spec.md)
- [Direct Messaging](mdc:docs/features/direct-messaging/direct-messaging.spec.md)
- User Profiles, Group Chat, Real-time Presence, Push Notifications, Admin Functionality

## Acceptance Criteria
Follow the specific acceptance criteria defined in the PRD:
- Functional requirements (95% test case pass rate)
- Performance targets (messages <2s, presence <5s)
- Reliability goals (50+ concurrent users)
- User experience standards (70% profile completion)

## Development Workflow
1. Read the feature specification thoroughly
2. Implement data models and Firebase rules first
3. Create UI components following design patterns
4. Add real-time functionality with proper cleanup
5. Implement error handling and loading states
6. Test across different user scenarios
7. Verify acceptance criteria before moving to next feature